Correcting my previous pass on the reviewer's three substantive points: (a) I replaced the inert name-filter with an executable probe run via `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run` (never `pnpm test --`, which routes filters into cac's `--` bucket and sweeps the whole suite); at HEAD it is 2 failed / 1 passed, under the patch 3 passed — an exit-status difference, not a match artifact. (b) I exercised the blocked-walk path with a purpose-built 3-stage `walkblock` process (g1 clean, g2 blocking command gate): at HEAD the gate-blocked `advance --to g2 --commit` commits spec.md/story.md/telemetry and leaves `?? .bklg/foundation/cutover/root/_review.md`, confirming the `BlockedWalkError` catch at advance.ts:220 is a second, independent instance of the same defect. (c) I narrowed the file set by patching `src/cli/advance.ts` ALONE (deriving the dir via `locateItem(root, id)?.dir`, both staging sites) with `src/process/engine.ts` byte-identical to HEAD: `tsc --noEmit` clean and all three probes green. The engine faithfully reports what the transition wrote and the spec explicitly leaves `writtenPaths`' meaning unchanged, so `AdvanceResult.itemDir` is the chosen fix shape, not the origin of the wrong behaviour — engine.ts is dropped from the root cause.

Boundary and regression evidence: a sibling story's `_stray.md` (planted in that item's own directory, which no existing test does) stays out of the commit and remains untracked in both worlds; the telemetry partition stays in the commit in both worlds (AC-003 additive holds); under the patch the existing suite is 5 passed / 1 failed with the single failure being the "narrow staging" test the spec mandates inverting, and the RK-N0001 gitignored-path regression (AC-004) stays green. `src/git/index.ts`'s `commit()` is exonerated — its `git add -- <dir>` recursed into the item directory correctly and unmodified. The scratch patch and probe file were reverted; `git status --porcelain` is empty.","discriminating_test":"test/zz-issue77-probe.test.ts (I authored, ran, and then removed it to keep the tree clean; recreate to reproduce). Invoke as `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run test/zz-issue77-probe.test.ts` — NOT `pnpm test -- ...`, which puts every filter into cac's `--` bucket and runs the full suite. Three cases, all scaffolding a real git repo + `redkiln init` + initiative/project/story, committing the scaffold, then: (1) SINGLE-STEP — write `_review.md` into the story's own dir, run `advance <id> --to g1 --commit`, assert `git show --stat --name-only --pretty=format: HEAD` CONTAINS `_review.md`; (2) BLOCKED WALK — same, but on a 3-stage `walkblock` process whose g2 carries `gate: { kind: command, run: "node -e \"process.exit(1)\"", blocking: true }`, run `advance <id> --to g2 --commit` (exits 1) and assert the cleared-hop commit CONTAINS `_review.md`; (3) BOUNDARY — a second story `sib` under the same project with `_stray.md` in ITS dir, advance the first story, assert the commit does NOT contain `_stray.md`, that `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all` still does, and that the commit DOES contain the `.redkiln/telemetry/events` partition. Observed at HEAD: (1) and (2) FAIL ("expected '.bklg/foundation/cutover/root/spec.md…' to contain '_review.md'", file left `??`), (3) passes. Observed with a patch confined to src/cli/advance.ts (both staging sites prepend `locateItem(root, id)?.dir`), src/process/engine.ts untouched: all 3 pass, `tsc --noEmit` clean. Case (3) passing identically in both worlds is what discriminates "too-narrow staging set in advance.ts" from "staging is repo-wide/over-broad" or "commit() mishandles pathspecs"; case (2) discriminates a one-site fix from the two-site defect; the engine-untouched control discriminates advance.ts as the origin from engine.ts as a co-cause.","root_cause":{"summary":"`src/cli/advance.ts` builds the `--commit` staging pathspec set from the transition's own `writtenPaths` alone — `result.writtenPaths.filter(existsSync)` at the applied-advance commit (~line 123) and `err.writtenPaths.filter(existsSync)` in the `BlockedWalkError` catch (~line 220) — so companion artifacts already sitting in the item's own directory (a `_review.md`, a `_discovery/` corpus) are never staged and stay untracked behind a commit that reports `gitCommitted: true`. Both sites are the same defect and both must widen to include the item's directory; the promised broadening was never implemented anywhere in the tree (no `itemDir` in src/ or dist/, no CHANGELOG entry, tests still pre-fix).","files":["src/cli/advance.ts"]}}

