idence is undercounted: `grep -rn CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT commands/` returns 20 matches across 6 files, not the 12 the root cause asserts — 12 is only the shared note lines (2 x 6), and the 8 `scriptPath` placeholder lines the summary says are included in that number are not.","evidence":"reproduced","rationale":"I ran the exact command the hypothesis cites and counted per file. The spec itself says "20 references ... 12 are the shared note ... 8 are the actual Workflow({ scriptPath ...}) invocation lines", so the hypothesis conflated a sub-count with the total while presenting it as the grep's output.","files":["commands/closeout.md","commands/fix.md","commands/implement.md","commands/initiative.md","commands/kb-ingest.md","commands/plan.md"],"repro":{"command":"grep -rn CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT commands/ | wc -l; grep -rc CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT commands/*.md","observed":"20; closeout.md:3 fix.md:3 implement.md:3 init.md:0 initiative.md:3 kb-ingest.md:3 plan.md:5","expected_when_met":"0 matches, grep exits 1."}},{"ac":"AC-001","claim":"The named discriminating test does not discriminate: with the defect FULLY FIXED (command implemented, all six commands/*.md cleaned, AC-001/002/003 satisfied), `npx vitest run test/workflow-root.test.ts` still fails with byte-identical output and exit 1.","evidence":"reproduced","rationale":"I applied the substantive fix (bundledWorkflowsDir + src/cli/workflow-root.ts + COMMANDS entry + dispatch case + prose rewrite in all six commands/*.md), verified the command prints the absolute workflows dir and that grep returns zero matches, then re-ran the discriminator. It produced "No test files found, exiting with code 1" — identical to the run offered as proof the fix is absent. The check is a file-existence probe, so it cannot separate "nothing landed" from "everything that fixes the defect landed, minus the test file". Tree reverted to clean afterwards.","files":["test/workflow-root.test.ts","src/cli/workflow-root.ts","commands/fix.md"],"repro":{"command":"# with fix applied but no test file:
