rt would contain filled TDD/gate/commit rows and the quoted line numbers, and the suite count would match the run."}},{"ac":"AC-004","claim":"docs/src/content/docs/reference/cli.mdx has no `## workflow-root` section and CHANGELOG.md's [Unreleased] has no `Added` entry naming #70, as the hypothesis states.","evidence":"reproduced","rationale":"Read the heading index of the docs page and the Unreleased block directly; both gaps are as described.","files":["docs/src/content/docs/reference/cli.mdx","CHANGELOG.md"],"repro":{"command":"grep -n '^## ' docs/src/content/docs/reference/cli.mdx | tail -3; awk '/^## \[Unreleased\]/,/^## \[[0-9]/' CHANGELOG.md | grep -n '^### '","observed":"809: ## `record-links` / 873: ## See also (no workflow-root section); Unreleased has only '### Fixed' and '### Pack changes / migration'","expected_when_met":"A `## workflow-root` section between `## record-links` and `## See also`, and an `### Added` entry naming #70."}},{"ac":"AC-003","claim":"The root cause's localization to "the six commands/*.md files" is incomplete: the same unfollowable `$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` launch instruction also lives inside workflows/forge-initiative.js, and forge-closeout.js resolves a template asset under it, so fixing exactly the named set leaves a live instance of the defect.","evidence":"advisory","rationale":"I observed the text by grep, but I cannot show it changes the outcome at a stronger bar: the spec's frozen boundary explicitly puts "any change to the 8 workflows/forge-*.js scripts" out of scope, and forge-closeout.js's use has an explicit documented fallback. Flagging as a scope gap in the hypothesis's causal story rather than a defect in it.","files":["workflows/forge-initiative.js","workflows/forge-closeout.js"],"repro":{"command":"grep -rn CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT workflows/","observed":"forge-initiative.js:6 'Launch by `scriptPath: $CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/workflows/forge-initiative.js` (the pinned plugin copy), not by `name` ...'; forge-closeout.js:1045-1046 resolves `$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/workflows/_templates/completion-audit-format.md`","expected_when_met":"Either these carry the same `redkiln workflow-root` resolution, or the root cause states explicitly that they are knowingly left broken."}},{"ac":"AC-001","claim":"Four of the ten files named as the root cause (src/store/paths.ts, src/cli/workflow-root.ts, src/cli/commands.ts, src/cli/index.ts) contain no defective code — they are remedy sites, and one of them does not exist — so the file set mixes "where the wrong behaviour originates" with "where the fix would go".","evidence":"advisory","rationale":"For an omission fault this conflation is defensible and still actionable, and the causal six (commands/*.md) are named first and correctly, so I will not claim it mislocates. I could not evidence any harm from the over-listing beyond it being a restatement of the spec's frozen-boundary table rather than an independently derived localization.","files":["src/cli/workflow-root.ts","src/cli/commands.ts","src/cli/index.ts","src/store/paths.ts"],"repro":{"command":"ls src/cli/workflow-root.ts; git log --oneline -1 -- src/cli/commands.ts src/cli/index.ts src/store/paths.ts","observed":"src/cli/workflow-root.ts: No such file or directory; the three existing files are unmodified since the single 'advance to implement' commit and contain nothing that produces the wrong behaviour","expected_when_met":"A root cause names the origin of the wrong value; these files would be listed as the fix surface, distinct from the causal set."}}],"boundary_respected":true,"rubric":[{"dimension":"ac-coverage","score":0,"rationale":"None of AC-001..AC-005 is met. `redkiln workflow-root` is an unknown command (AC-001, AC-002), `grep -rn CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT commands/` returns 20 matches rather than zero (AC-003), cli.mdx has no `## workflow-root` section (AC-004), and AC-005 is only vacuously satisfied because nothing changed. The hypothesis's central assertion — none of RK-S0232 landed — reproduces exactly."},{"dimension":"boundary-fidelity","score":3,"rationale":"Vacuously perfect: the working tree is a single clean commit with no stash, no other branch and no second worktree, so zero files were touched, inside or outside the frozen boundary. I temporarily patched boundary files to test the discriminator and reverted; `git status --short` is empty."},{"dimension":"test-integrity","score":0,"rationale":"test/workflow-root.test.ts does not exist, and the named discriminator is a file-existence probe in both directions: it still exits 1 with identical output after I fully fixed the defect, and it exits 0 on a seven-line stub while the command is still unknown and all 20 env-var references remain. flag-projection.test.ts and index.ts's `name satisfies never` guard are both keyed off the COMMANDS array, so an absent entry produces no case and no compile error — nothing in the repo can observe the omission."},{"dimension":"gate-greenness","score":3,"rationale":"The merge gate is genuinely green and I ran all of it: `tsc --noEmit` exit 0, `eslint .` exit 0, `prettier --check .` clean, `vitest run` 92 files / 1881 tests passed. The greenness is uninformative rather than earned — it is green over an empty diff — but as a measured fact the gates pass."},{"dimension":"regression-risk","score":3,"rationale":"Zero diff means zero regression surface; every existing command, test and help text is untouched. The standing risk is the unfixed #70 defect itself (six commands still instruct the orchestrator to resolve an env var that is empty in both shell tools, plus a seventh live instance in workflows/forge-initiative.js), which is scored under ac-coverage, not here."}]}

